WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Speaker 1: as if you didn't already suspect&nbsp;
that Nikki Haley's 2024 Republican presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:11.160
campaign was off to a bad start. We've learned&nbsp;
that she has been dramatically overstating the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:18.060
amount of money she has raised and the campaign&nbsp;
looks to be, I don't want to say dead on arrival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.760
but very, very close. So The Washington&nbsp;
Post reporting Nikki Haley's campaign vastly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:30.060
overstating her fundraising. Listen to this.&nbsp;
Instead of the $11 million touted by her campaign,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:37.620
Haley brought in about 8.3 million. Not all&nbsp;
of which can even be used for the presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:44.760
campaign. They had been talking about 11 million&nbsp;
in six weeks. But now that the filings have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:52.380
made with the FEC, that was an over exaggeration.&nbsp;
The campaign appears to have double counted money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:58.200
It moved among various committees, committees.&nbsp;
The filings covering the first three months of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:04.560
the year show that three committees affiliated&nbsp;
with Haley collectively brought in 8.3 million.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:15.060
Haley's joint fundraising committee raised about&nbsp;
4.4 million. The campaign committee's haul of 5.1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.040
million included 1.8 million from that other&nbsp;
committee. So a bunch of that money was double&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:27.300
counted. And this is all being considered highly&nbsp;
unusual. The Trump campaign Saturday said they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:33.780
brought in about 14 and a half million and then&nbsp;
another 4.3 million into the leadership PAC and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.300
on and on and on. Now, the funniest part of this&nbsp;
is not all of that 8.3 million can actually be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:46.800
used for the campaign because the leadership&nbsp;
PAC is typically only to boost allies or to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:53.640
promote a message not directly to finance her&nbsp;
own campaign. So, listen, this is pretty bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.920
This is pretty bad. And there's two ways to&nbsp;
interpret this. One way to interpret it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:06.360
the fact that Nikki even raised eight, even though&nbsp;
she can only use a fraction of it. That's already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:13.740
amazing for a candidate who isn't doing that well&nbsp;
in the polls. The counterpoint would be this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:20.520
probably the most attention she will ever get.&nbsp;
This was the big moment, and she still wasn't able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:26.820
to raise that much money and it didn't do anything&nbsp;
for her in the polling. And indeed, the polling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:34.980
doesn't look very good. Her best poll right now&nbsp;
is a particular Iowa poll which which has her in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.560
third place at 14% behind Trump and a guy who's&nbsp;
not even running yet, Ron DeSantis, that's her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:48.120
best showing. Most polling has Nikki Haley at two,&nbsp;
three or 4%, for example, in the Kentucky primary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:55.680
She's at 4% in the Georgia primary. She is at&nbsp;
4%. So a couple of different thoughts here. One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:02.640
I don't think we had to wait for these numbers&nbsp;
from both polling and fundraising to be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:09.180
say this campaign's probably not going anywhere.&nbsp;
At the same time, there's the perspective that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:15.420
campaign doesn't really need to go anywhere in the&nbsp;
sense that Nikki Haley. I mean, listen, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:21.780
people have asked me before when someone like&nbsp;
Nikki Haley announces, given what the polling is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:27.300
does Nikki Haley actually think she can win? I&nbsp;
don't know the answer. I've never actually asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:34.800
these candidates. Do. You don't really think you&nbsp;
can win, do you? I'm sure she wouldn't admit it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:41.520
if she didn't think she could win. But there's a&nbsp;
particularly unique situation in this in this 2024&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:48.300
Republican primary, which is Nikki Haley could be&nbsp;
running as an audition for VP. That's something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.080
that's been discussed and that I think should be&nbsp;
considered and not ruled out. Sure, she might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:04:01.440
running for VP. Trump certainly seems to think&nbsp;
that she is. And also there is the usefulness of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.840
more candidates to Trump, because when you look&nbsp;
at 2024 polling, one of the things that you'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.840
notice is in head to head matchups between Trump&nbsp;
and DeSantis, DeSantis does better, not better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.700
than Trump. He's still mostly losing to Trump,&nbsp;
but he does better than when you have. Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:24.420
DeSantis, Haley Pence, Tim Scott, Vivek Ramaswamy,&nbsp;
and whoever else. The more candidates you have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:30.900
the better it actually is for Trump. So&nbsp;
there's also the speculation or the idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:37.260
that Trump liked the idea of Nikki Haley running&nbsp;
because it actually helps him. Needless to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:43.920
this is a campaign that, as a presidential&nbsp;
campaign, was doomed from day one as a vice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:49.080
presidential audition remains to be&nbsp;
seen. And we will indeed see that.

